---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Legal notice" description="Legal notice and privacy information.">
  <div class="wrap content-page">
    <h1>Legal notice &amp; privacy</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>This page is a placeholder.</strong> Before the site goes
      live and starts taking enquiries or sales, replace this with an
      actual legal notice and privacy policy. In Luxembourg and the wider
      EU that typically means:
    </p>
    <p>
      A legal notice ("mentions légales") naming the business or individual
      operating the site, a postal address, a contact email, and — if
      applicable — a business registration (RCS) number and VAT number.
    </p>
    <p>
      A privacy policy describing what personal data the site collects (for
      example, names and email addresses submitted through the contact
      form), why, how long it's kept, and how someone can request it be
      deleted, in line with GDPR.
    </p>
    <p>
      If the site sells work directly, terms of sale covering pricing,
      shipping, and the buyer's right of withdrawal should also be added.
      An accountant or lawyer familiar with Luxembourg small-business rules
      can confirm exactly what applies here.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
